.el .ds Aq '
.TH mtr-ng 1  "mtr-ng 0.3.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mtr\-ng \- A modern implementation of mtr (My Traceroute) with unicode and terminal graphics
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmtr\-ng\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-count\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-M\fR|\fB\-\-max\-hops\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-report\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-csv\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-numeric\fR] [\fB\-z\fR|\fB\-\-aslookup\fR] [\fB\-\-sparkline\-scale\fR] [\fB\-\-ema\-alpha\fR] [\fB\-\-fields\fR] [\fB\-\-show\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-simulate\fR] [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-protocol\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fITARGET\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
A modern implementation of mtr (My Traceroute) with unicode and terminal graphics
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-count\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR
Number of rounds to run (default: until quit; 10 in report mode)
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<INTERVAL>\fR [default: 1000]
Time between rounds in milliseconds (at least 100, except with \-\-simulate)
.TP
\fB\-M\fR, \fB\-\-max\-hops\fR \fI<MAX_HOPS>\fR [default: 30]
Maximum number of hops (1\-255)
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-report\fR
Enable report mode (non\-interactive)
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Report as JSON, with mtr\*(Aqs field names (implies \-\-report)
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-csv\fR
Report as CSV, one row per hop (implies \-\-report)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-numeric\fR
Show IP addresses instead of hostnames
.TP
\fB\-z\fR, \fB\-\-aslookup\fR
Show the AS number of each hop. Asks Team Cymru\*(Aqs DNS about every public address
.TP
\fB\-\-sparkline\-scale\fR \fI<SPARKLINE_SCALE>\fR [default: logarithmic]
Sparkline scaling mode: linear or logarithmic (default: logarithmic)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
linear
.IP \(bu 2
logarithmic
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ema\-alpha\fR \fI<EMA_ALPHA>\fR [default: 0.1]
Smoothing factor for the EMA column, above 0 and at most 1. Higher follows recent RTTs faster
.TP
\fB\-\-fields\fR \fI<FIELDS>\fR
Select which columns to display (default: hop,host,loss,sent,last,avg,ema,best,worst,graph)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
hop: Hop number
.IP \(bu 2
host: Hostname/IP address
.IP \(bu 2
asn: Origin AS number (looked up with \-\-aslookup)
.IP \(bu 2
loss: Packet loss percentage
.IP \(bu 2
sent: Number of packets sent
.IP \(bu 2
last: Last RTT measurement
.IP \(bu 2
avg: Average RTT
.IP \(bu 2
ema: Exponential moving average RTT
.IP \(bu 2
jitter: Last jitter value
.IP \(bu 2
jitter\-avg: Average jitter
.IP \(bu 2
best: Best (minimum) RTT
.IP \(bu 2
worst: Worst (maximum) RTT
.IP \(bu 2
stdev: Standard deviation of the RTT
.IP \(bu 2
graph: RTT sparkline graph
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-all\fR
Display all available columns
.TP
\fB\-\-simulate\fR
Show fake data instead of probing (for demos and testing); marked SIMULATED
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-protocol\fR \fI<PROTOCOL>\fR [default: icmp]
Probe protocol (only icmp is implemented so far)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
icmp: ICMP Echo (ping) \- default and most common
.IP \(bu 2
udp: UDP probes (not implemented yet)
.IP \(bu 2
tcp: TCP SYN probes (not implemented yet)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Report mode: print errors only, no warnings
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Append debug logs to this file (level can be overridden with RUST_LOG)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fITARGET\fR>
Target hostname or IP address
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q
Quit (also Ctrl\-C)
.TP
.B ?
Show or hide this help
.TP
.B o
Choose and order columns
.TP
.B r
Reset statistics
.TP
.B h
Host names or IP addresses
.TP
.B s
Linear or logarithmic RTT scale
.TP
.B v
Sparkline or heatmap
.TP
.B c
Cycle colour modes
.TP
.B ↑ k
Select previous hop
.TP
.B ↓ j
Select next hop
.TP
.B PgUp
Scroll up a page
.TP
.B PgDn
Scroll down a page
.TP
.B Home
First hop
.TP
.B End
Last hop
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the selection
.SH COLUMNS
Pick them with \fB\-\-fields\fR, or with \fBo\fR while running. Times are in milliseconds.
.TP
.B hop
Hop number
.TP
.B host
Host name or address
.TP
.B asn
Autonomous system
.TP
.B loss
Packet loss
.TP
.B sent
Probes sent
.TP
.B last
Last RTT
.TP
.B avg
Average RTT
.TP
.B ema
Smoothed RTT (EMA)
.TP
.B jitter
Last jitter
.TP
.B jitter\-avg
Average jitter
.TP
.B best
Best RTT
.TP
.B worst
Worst RTT
.TP
.B stdev
RTT standard deviation
.TP
.B graph
RTT history graph
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B mtr\-ng example.com
Trace interactively until q.
.TP
.B mtr\-ng \-r example.com
Print a report after 10 rounds.
.TP
.B mtr\-ng \-r \-c 100 \-n 1.1.1.1
A 100\-round report without DNS.
.TP
.B mtr\-ng \-\-fields hop,host,loss,avg,graph example.com
Show fewer columns.
.TP
.B mtr\-ng \-i 500 example.com
Probe every 500 ms.
.TP
.B mtr\-ng \-\-simulate example.com
Fake data, marked SIMULATED.
.SH PRIVILEGES
On macOS mtr\-ng needs no privileges: it uses unprivileged ICMP sockets. On Linux it needs root or the CAP_NET_RAW capability (setcap cap_net_raw+ep "$(command \-v mtr\-ng)"). Windows is not supported yet. Only ICMP over IPv4 is implemented; IPv6 targets and other protocols exit with an error.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
https://github.com/edejong\-dbc/mtr\-ng/issues
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mtr (8),
